A chain whose only possible break points are its own `:` boundaries is
left over-long rather than split; method-call links (`:GetItem(1)`) are
part of the chain too (fmt.atomic_property_chains "If the only way to
satisfy the limit would be splitting a chain, the line is left over-long
instead").
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Touch;
:PARAMETERS oConfigurationManagerInstance;
DoSomething(oConfigurationManagerInstance:databaseConnectionSettings:primaryConnectionString);
oConfigurationManagerInstance:connectionPool:GetItem(1):lastUsedConnectionDescriptor:Reset();
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Touch;
	:PARAMETERS oConfigurationManagerInstance;

	DoSomething(oConfigurationManagerInstance:databaseConnectionSettings:primaryConnectionString);
	oConfigurationManagerInstance:connectionPool:GetItem(1):lastUsedConnectionDescriptor:Reset();
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
3:1-3:12 warning direct_procedure_call: 'DoSomething' is not a known built-in function or in-file procedure. If it is a custom procedure, dispatch it via DoProc/ExecFunction; if it is a legacy vendor built-in, this call is valid as written.
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
2:13-2:42 info identifier_too_long: Variable name 'oConfigurationManagerInstance' exceeds 20-character limit (effective length 28 excluding prefix)
3:1-3:12 warning direct_procedure_call: 'DoSomething' is not a known built-in function or in-file procedure. If it is a custom procedure, dispatch it via DoProc/ExecFunction; if it is a legacy vendor built-in, this call is valid as written.
